You can compare strings using Bash.

#!/bin/bash

USERNAME="bilal"

if [ "$USERNAME" = "bilal" ]; then
    echo "Username matched"
else
    echo "Username does not match"
fi

=> Common string operators
=       Equal
!=      Not equal
-z      String is empty
-n      String is not empty

Eg:
#!/bin/bash

PASSWORD="admin"

if [ -z "$PASSWORD" ]; then
    echo "Password is empty"
else
    echo "Password is not empty"
fi
